Tissue Weather is released under two licences.

CODE — MIT (the full text follows). This covers everything executable or
structural in the repository: src/, tools/, tests/, blender/, index.html,
dist/, the build and CI configuration.

COURSE TEXT — Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0),
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/. This covers the teaching prose:
docs/TEACHING.md, docs/MODEL.md, docs/SPEC.md, docs/EXTENDING.md,
docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, docs/tissues/*.md, README.md, and the student-facing copy
carried in the code (src/copy.js, the `copy` block of each tissue definition in
src/tissues/, and the teaching text in index.html). Reuse it in your own course
with attribution; the MIT terms below apply to it as well, so you may also take
it as MIT if that is simpler for you.

Cited literature quoted or paraphrased in the documentation remains the property
of its authors and publishers; the DOIs are given so you can go to the sources.

